{
  "id": "07512_shibushibu",
  "headword": "しぶしぶ",
  "reading": "しぶしぶ",
  "part_of_speech": "adverb",
  "gloss": "reluctantly; unwillingly",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "reluctantly; unwillingly; grudgingly",
      "explanation": "Doing something while showing resistance or lack of enthusiasm. Implies going along with something despite not wanting to."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "07512_shibushibu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}はしぶしぶ{承諾|しょうだく}した。",
      "english": "He reluctantly agreed.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "07512_shibushibu_ex2",
      "japanese": "しぶしぶながら{手伝|てつだ}ってくれた。",
      "english": "They helped me, albeit reluctantly.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "07512_shibushibu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{子|こ}どもはしぶしぶ{宿題|しゅくだい}を{始|はじ}めた。",
      "english": "The child reluctantly started their homework.",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "MIMETIC ORIGIN:\nReduplicated form related to {渋|しぶ}い (astringent, reluctant). The repetition emphasizes the reluctance.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・しぶしぶ{承諾|しょうだく}する - to agree reluctantly\n・しぶしぶ{従|したが}う - to comply unwillingly\n・しぶしぶ{受|う}け{入|い}れる - to accept grudgingly\n・しぶしぶながら - albeit reluctantly\n\nPOSITION:\nAppears before the verb, modifying the manner of action.\n\nSIMILAR EXPRESSIONS:\n・{嫌々|いやいや} - unwillingly (stronger negative feeling)\n・{仕方|しかた}なく - having no choice\n・{渋々|しぶしぶ} - alternative kanji spelling",
